# Ownership by team (ADR A, decision 10; the registry is osp/teams.yaml in
# build-kit). Hydrosphere capability, discipline Terrestrial Hydrology. One
# person occupies every team during the interim solo period.
* @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# The domain bundle.
/knowledge/       @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# Methods stewardship (the third steward type the architecture document
# records): recipes and attested computations that combine several
# providers' products are owned by the methods stewards, not by any one
# product's steward.
/knowledge/recipes/       @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-methods-stewards
/knowledge/computations/  @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-methods-stewards

# Per-producer path scopes.
#
# The bundle names its concepts by the producer of the thing they
# describe (usgs-, nwis-, nldi- for the water agency; imerg-, nldas2-
# and gesdisc- for that data centre; mod16- for the land processes one;
# swot- and hydrocron- for the ocean one; openet- and snodas- for the
# rest). Those prefixes are what make single-producer stewardship
# possible: a steward at one agency can own the rules about their own
# products without owning anyone else's, and derive_credit reads each
# scope and lists it beside the steward it maps to.
#
# A scope resolves to its producer's steward team where that team exists
# (the ocean data centre's does) and to the sphere maintainers until it
# does; accepting a steward is then a team membership change, or the
# creation of the producer's team in build-kit's registry and a one-line
# change here.

# The water agency: gauges, the peaks record, basin delineation and the
# hydrologic units.
/knowledge/**/usgs-*   @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers
/knowledge/**/nwis-*   @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers
/knowledge/**/nldi-*   @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# The precipitation and land-surface forcing data centre.
/knowledge/**/imerg-*    @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers
/knowledge/**/nldas2-*   @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers
/knowledge/**/gesdisc-*  @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# The land processes data centre: evapotranspiration.
/knowledge/**/mod16-*  @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# The ocean data centre: the surface water mission and its time series
# service. Note that the mission's own product concepts live in the
# provider bundle and are owned there; what this scope covers is this
# plugin's use of them.
/knowledge/**/swot-*       @open-science-pillars/podaac-stewards
/knowledge/**/hydrocron-*  @open-science-pillars/podaac-stewards

# The soil moisture mission.
/knowledge/**/smap-*  @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# The evapotranspiration service, the snow assimilation, and the
# reservoir survey tables.
/knowledge/**/openet-*       @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers
/knowledge/**/snodas-*       @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers
/knowledge/**/reclamation-*  @open-science-pillars/hydrosphere-maintainers

# Runtime projections (ADR B): the Claude package files are the Cowork
# projection of .osp/package.yaml and belong to the runtime maintainers.
/.claude-plugin/  @open-science-pillars/runtime-cowork-maintainers
/.mcp.json        @open-science-pillars/runtime-cowork-maintainers
